// DeckPulse — explore the GateReadings table after local-file ingestion.
// Run these in the default queryset attached to the DeckPulseEventhouse KQL database.
// Run one query at a time.

// 1. Confirm every sample row arrived. Expected: 6,000.
GateReadings
| count

// 2. Preview a handful of rows and check that the columns look right.
GateReadings
| take 10

// 3. Average occupancy and number of readings per deck.
GateReadings
| summarize AvgOccupancyPct = avg(OccupancyPct), Readings = count() by Deck
| order by AvgOccupancyPct desc

// 4. Near-full spikes. Status is ALERT when OccupancyPct is above 88.
GateReadings
| where Status == "ALERT"
| project Timestamp, GateId, Deck, OccupancyPct
| order by Timestamp asc

// 5. ALERT count by deck so the ops brief has a watch order.
GateReadings
| where Status == "ALERT"
| summarize Alerts = count() by Deck
| order by Alerts desc

// 6. Inspect the stored schema, including column types.
.show table GateReadings schema as json
